  Copyright (C) 2026 OpenMasjid-Solutions

  The app theme — DARK IN BOTH SYSTEM MODES. This XML theme only governs the brief pre-Compose window
  (background + system bars); all real theming is done in Compose via SakinaTheme, and MainActivity
  forces SakinaTheme(darkTheme = true) because the kiosk is a dark-by-design giving station.

  This used to be a light theme with a dark variant under values-night/, which followed the TABLET's
  system setting rather than the kiosk's: on a tablet left in light mode every cold start painted a
  pale window, with dark status-bar icons, before the dark kiosk drew over it — the native form of
  the "flash of the wrong theme" the design spec's first-paint rule exists to prevent. The window now
  matches what Compose will draw, so there is nothing for a night variant to vary, and there is none.

  Parented on the platform Material theme so we pull in no extra support library — Compose supplies
  Material 3 itself.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.OpenMasjidKiosk" parent="android:Theme.Material.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/surface_dark</item>
        <item name="android:statusBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <item name="android:navigationBarColor">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <item name="android:windowLightStatusBar">false</item>
    </style>
</resources>
